## Team lessons

TEAM LESSON · #repo/export-service
Export jobs are idempotent, keyed by job_id
Learned from @ben's review · 18d ago
Re-running an export with the same `job_id` must produce the same files and never duplicate rows. See [[money-integer-cents]] for totals.

TEAM LESSON · #team/data-pipelines
Tag every row with lab_customer_id
Learned from @ben's review · 20d ago
Every row that enters a pipeline carries `lab_customer_id`. Pipelines reject untagged rows instead of guessing. Makes [[sec-lab-isolation]] checkable in code.

TEAM LESSON · #repo/export-service
Stream uploads; never buffer a full export
Learned from @emily's correction · 7d ago · approved by @ben
Stream export files to storage in chunks. Buffering a full export OOM-killed the worker twice.

TEAM LESSON · #org
Money and payouts are integer cents
Learned from @ben's review · 12d ago · approved by @greg
Store and compute every payout as integer cents (`amount_cents`). Never floats, never dollars. Learned from @ben's review on #repo/export-service. Related: [[export-idempotent]].

TEAM LESSON · #org
Migrations are append-only
Learned from @ben's review · 15d ago · approved by @greg
Never edit a migration that has run anywhere. Add a new one. Owner: @ben.

TEAM LESSON · #org
Use logger, not console.log
Learned from @kevin's correction · 9d ago · approved by @greg
Use the shared `logger` (structured, PII-scrubbed). `console.log` bypasses scrubbing and breaks [[sec-no-pii-logs]]. First taught by @kevin, confirmed by @nick on #team/evals.

## Who to ask

Ask @ben about export-service. @ben owns #repo/export-service. Ping before changing the export format or schedule.

